# Echo top-10 (Tom Slemen)
a("Murdered miller at Bidston Windmill","ghost","","Bidston Windmill, Bidston Hill","Bidston Windmill, Wirral","A misty outline of a man, said to be a miller murdered in the early 1800s, has been reported many times around the windmill on Bidston Hill. Local lore also ties the hill to covens and a buried occultist named Richard Tilly.","Liverpool Echo (Tom Slemen)",E1,["apparition","rural","open-to-visit"])
a("Dark disc photographed over Bidston Hill","craft","2012/07","Bidston Hill, Birkenhead","Bidston Observatory, Wirral","Engineer Mike Dunne, 25, photographed a dark disc-shaped object hovering over houses near Bidston Hill before it vanished; dozens of others were said to have seen it. Slemen calls the hill a UFO 'window area'.","Liverpool Echo (Tom Slemen)",E1,["photo","multiple-witnesses","urban"])
a("Golden car vanishing into Queensway Tunnel wall","timeslip","","Queensway Tunnel, Birkenhead-Liverpool","Queensway Tunnel, Liverpool","Drivers have described a golden, futuristic-looking vehicle overtaking at huge speed and disappearing into the tunnel wall, alongside an old 1960s-style police car seen in the early hours. Slemen lists the tunnel as a timeslip spot.","Liverpool Echo (Tom Slemen)",E1,["road","urban"])
a("John Lennon at the Mendips window","ghost","","Mendips, 251 Menlove Avenue, Woolton","251 Menlove Avenue, Liverpool","Beatles fans have reported a white-suited Lennon looking out of the bedroom window of his childhood home after it was restored by the National Trust. One fan claimed a night-vision camera caught a figure at the window.","Liverpool Echo (Tom Slemen)",E1,["house","apparition","photo","open-to-visit"])
a("Broken-neck man in the Epstein Theatre","ghost","1993/02","Epstein Theatre, Hanover Street, Liverpool","Epstein Theatre, Liverpool","A pale man with his head lolling on his shoulder has been seen in the dressing rooms since the 1920s and is said to herald misfortune. In February 1993 a staging of The Devil Rides Out was reportedly plagued by disturbances after a pentagram was chalked on stage.","Liverpool Echo (Tom Slemen)",E1,["apparition","urban","open-to-visit"])
a("Flat WWI sergeant on the Birkenhead train","ghost","","James Street Station, Liverpool","James Street railway station, Liverpool","A strangely two-dimensional soldier with sergeant's stripes, a thin moustache and a swagger stick rides trains from Birkenhead Central and steps off at James Street. A lollipop man told Slemen he saw it in the 1990s with other passengers.","Liverpool Echo (Tom Slemen)",E1,["soldier","apparition","multiple-witnesses","urban"])
a("Knowsley Hall banshee and phantom cars","ghost","2009","Knowsley Hall, Knowsley","Knowsley Hall","A wailing woman in white with dark eye sockets is said to roam the grounds around 4am, and two driverless vintage cars with glaring headlamps haunt the estate roads. A Welsh paranormal group photographed an 'orb' there in 2009.","Liverpool Echo (Tom Slemen)",E1,["white-lady","road","house","photo"])
a("Huskisson's limping ghost, St James's Cemetery","ghost","","St James's Cemetery, Hope Street, Liverpool","St James' Gardens, Liverpool","William Huskisson MP, killed by Stephenson's Rocket in 1830, is said to limp from his mausoleum in the sunken cemetery below the Anglican Cathedral. The chalybeate spring there is linked in lore to a witch called Jenna Green.","Liverpool Echo (Tom Slemen)",E1,["apparition","urban","open-to-visit"])
a("Corpse candles of Bloody Acre, Childwall","lights","","Bloody Acre, All Saints Church, Childwall","All Saints Church, Childwall","A patch of scrub next to Liverpool's oldest church is said to be protected by an old promise never to build on it. Tales describe coloured orbs ('corpse candles'), 'black goblins' and a dark figure that rises before wars.","Liverpool Echo (Tom Slemen)",E1,["church","entity","urban"])
a("Lantern Jaw and the pyramid ghost, Rodney Street","ghost","","Rodney Street, Liverpool","Rodney Street, Liverpool","Slemen counts over forty ghosts on Rodney Street, including a caped, top-hatted figure called Lantern Jaw and a shorter man linked to William Mackenzie's pyramid tomb in St Andrew's churchyard, who are seen to argue. Phantom carriages are also heard.","Liverpool Echo (Tom Slemen)",E1,["apparition","urban"])
# hauntedplaces.org
a("Flat-capped worker at Cammell Laird","ghost","2004","Cammell Laird shipyard, Birkenhead","Cammell Laird, Birkenhead","A man in a flat cap and blue overalls is reported in the Construction Hall and an elderly woman near the kitchen. Staff have also described lights and doors operating by themselves and men in boiler suits vanishing.","HauntedPlaces.org",HP+"cammell-laird/",["apparition","urban"])
a("Father and son of Leasowe Castle","ghost","","Leasowe Castle, Moreton","Leasowe Castle","Legend says a man and his son were imprisoned here and the father killed the boy and then himself rather than starve; the pair are said to appear in the room where they died. The castle is now a hotel.","HauntedPlaces.org",HP+"leasowe-castle/",["castle","child","apparition","coast","open-to-visit"])
a("'It must have been Les' at the Royal Court","ghost","","Royal Court Theatre, Roe Street, Liverpool","Royal Court Theatre, Liverpool","A caretaker named Les is said to have fallen on the icy roof and died of exposure, and staff blame him for unexplained noises and figures in photos. A red-cardiganed old lady and a Cavalier have also been reported.","HauntedPlaces.org",HP+"royal-court-theatre-2/",["apparition","urban","open-to-visit"])
a("Bingo player at the old Gaumont, Dingle","ghost","","Gaumont Cinema, Park Road, Dingle","Gaumont Cinema, Princes Road, Liverpool","A woman who died during a bingo game is said to linger, still hoping to claim her winnings, along with a man who hanged himself behind the screen. Odd shadows and lights are reported.","HauntedPlaces.org",HP+"the-gaumont-cinema/",["apparition","urban"])
# Chester – hauntedrooms
a("Elizabeth Warburton of Stanley Palace","ghost","","Stanley Palace, Watergate Street, Chester","Stanley Palace, Chester","Former owner Elizabeth Warburton is seen walking through walls, alongside a Tudor-dressed man, a WWII officer and a grey-haired woman by the piano. Visitors report banging, crying children and footsteps.","Haunted Rooms",HR,["house","apparition","voices","open-to-visit"])
a("Marching legion under the George and Dragon","ghost","","George and Dragon, Liverpool Road, Chester","George and Dragon, Liverpool Road, Chester","The pub stands on the line of the Roman road out of the fortress, and landlords and drinkers have reported marching feet in the cellars following the old route. The pub closed in 2023.","Haunted Rooms",HR,["inn","soldier","voices","urban"])
# Echo recent
a("Apparition snapped at the old Crying Tree, Gateacre","ghost","2026/03","Former Crying Tree, Grange Lane, Gateacre","Grange Lane, Gateacre, Liverpool","A Haunted St Helens investigator says a friend's photo on the staircase of the derelict mansion-pub caught a figure passing between the banisters. She insists no mark on the wall explains it.","Liverpool Echo",LE+"ghost-appears-gateacre-pub-one-33701097",["photo","inn","investigated","urban"])
a("Basement presence at Clifton Hall, Birkenhead","ghost","2026","Clifton Hall, Clifton Road, Birkenhead","Clifton Road, Birkenhead","Volunteers and staff at the 1840s Masonic hall describe shadows, noises and a feeling of being watched in the basement, and visitors hear furniture dragged upstairs. Ghost-hunt bookings now help fund the building and Most Haunted filmed there.","Liverpool Echo",LE+"inside-historic-birkenhead-hall-drawing-33671716",["house","investigated","urban","open-to-visit"])
a("Vanishing passenger on Halsall Moss","ghost","1965","Gregory's Lane, Halsall Moss","Gregory Lane, Halsall","In early 1965 a driver on the Southport-Ormskirk road saw an elderly man in a flat cap sitting in the back of his Mini, who had gone when he leapt out. Years later another man described the same thing at the same bridge.","Liverpool Echo",LE+"chilling-mystery-halsall-mosss-phantom-34454804",["road","rural","apparition","multiple-witnesses"])
a("Bernie Brown on the Metropolitan Cathedral steps","ghost","1970s","Metropolitan Cathedral, Brownlow Hill, Liverpool","Liverpool Metropolitan Cathedral","The 'pauper's ghost' is linked to the workhouse that once stood here; in one 1970s account a man met a stranger whose head flopped back on a broken neck. A medium said Bernie died falling from a workhouse window.","Liverpool Echo",LE+"ghost-bernard-brown-said-haunt-34491410",["church","apparition","single-witness","urban"])
a("Coal-cellar boy of Calderstones House","ghost","2025","Calderstones House, Calderstones Park","Calderstones Mansion House, Liverpool","A Victorian boy crushed by a coal delivery is said to haunt the mansion; staff describe sickness after taunting him and footsteps along a corridor at night. The cellar is now sealed.","Liverpool Echo",LE+"ghost-boy-tragically-killed-christmas-33112037",["house","child","open-to-visit"])
a("The St Luke's abduction","timeslip","1991/12/20","St Luke's Church (Bombed-out Church), Liverpool","St Luke's Church, Liverpool","A six-year-old girl vanished from Bold Place behind the ruined church and was found holding the hand of a man in Victorian dress; she said an old woman in a shawl had led her inside. Researched by Tom Slemen.","Liverpool Echo",LE+"girl-6-vanished-during-shopping-34528628",["church","child","entity","urban"])
a("Childwall man whose family never existed","timeslip","1978","Fiveways Roundabout, Childwall","Fiveways, Childwall, Liverpool","After a crash at Fiveways while rushing his pregnant wife to hospital, a man woke to be told his wife and three children had never existed. Tom Slemen calls it one of his strangest cases; names were changed.","Liverpool Echo",LE+"liverpool-man-who-woke-car-34702069",["road","single-witness","urban"])
a("Glaring stranger at the Slaughter House pub","ghost","2002","Slaughter House, Fenwick Street, Liverpool","Slaughter House, Fenwick Street, Liverpool","In 2002 the landlord watched a man walk across the closed bar, glaring at him, then vanish. Later owners report a dark shadow on the back stairs and a lift bell ringing at 2am; Most Haunted visited in 2016.","Liverpool Echo",LE+"phantom-shadows-smashing-glasses-centuries-34642625",["inn","apparition","investigated","urban"])
a("Ghost girl on the Garston Loop Line","ghost","1980s","Liverpool Loop Line ('the Ralla'), Garston","Liverpool Loop Line, Garston","As a boy in the late 1980s, Haunted Scouse co-founder Chris Cummings saw a little girl on the old railway path who vanished with nowhere to go on the straight, open track.","Liverpool Echo",LE+"something-happened-peter-kavanaghs-cant-33873662",["child","single-witness","urban"])
a("Spring-heeled Jack in Everton","poltergeist","1904","William Henry Street, Everton","William Henry Street, Liverpool","In 1904 crowds gathered on William Henry Street after rumours of a 'Spring-heel Jack'; missiles were thrown at a house until the tenants left, though police found nothing. A leaping figure was also claimed on St Francis Xavier's church roof in 1888.","Liverpool Echo",LE+"tale-jumping-man-terrified-people-34611690",["objects-moved","police","multiple-witnesses","urban","entity"])
a("Screeching Ginny at Garston Dock station","ghost","1959/11/15","Old Garston Dock Station, Garston","Liverpool South Parkway","Children playing on the disused tracks were chased by a pale, witch-like figure that glided without moving its legs; one said her mouth opened impossibly wide. Lore names her as a jilted witch killed by a train.","Liverpool Echo",LE+"terrifying-tale-screeching-ginny-garstons-34676324",["child","entity","multiple-witnesses","urban"])
# Paranormal Database - Merseyside
a("Bonneted lady on Woodchurch Road","ghost","1905","Woodchurch Road, Birkenhead","Woodchurch Road, Birkenhead","An older woman in black with a bonnet appeared on the road and suddenly vanished; a newspaper said cyclists braked hard to avoid her. Others saw a small ball of fire that quickly disappeared.","Paranormal Database",PM+"index.php",["road","apparition","multiple-witnesses","urban"])
a("John Bibby's headless coach, Bootle","ghost","","Bibby's Lane / Peel Road, Bootle","Bibbys Lane, Bootle","Every New Year's Eve, local lore says, John Bibby drives his coach along the lane with his severed head in his lap.","Paranormal Database",PM+"index.php",["road","urban"])
a("Grey Lady of Ince Woods","ghost","","A565 through Ince Woods, Ince Blundell","Ince Woods, Ince Blundell","A woman is said to appear by a round house at midnight in front of traffic on the A565, causing crashes. She may be linked to a lady who took her life on nearby Park Wall Road.","Paranormal Database",PM+"index.php",["grey-lady","road","rural"])
a("'The Sarge' at the Woolton ambulance centre","poltergeist","1974","Quarry Street, Woolton","Quarry Street, Woolton, Liverpool","Ambulance crews blamed footsteps, broken windows and doors that unlocked themselves on 'the Sarge', a policeman killed when his patrol wagon hit a bollard.","Paranormal Database",PM+"index.php",["objects-moved","multiple-witnesses","urban"])
a("Perfume and shadows in the Western Approaches bunker","ghost","","Western Approaches (Battle of the Atlantic bunker), Liverpool","Western Approaches Museum, Liverpool","A visitor smelt perfume where a Wren reputedly fell to her death, saw shadows and felt followed. Figures in naval uniform are said to walk through the walls.","Paranormal Database",PM+"index.php",["military","single-witness","urban","open-to-visit"])
a("Floating torso of Lime Street","ghost","1990s","Lime Street, Liverpool","Lime Street, Liverpool","A tall figure with no visible legs and a silently moving mouth has been reported along Lime Street, with sightings said to go back centuries.","Paranormal Database",PM+"?pageNum_paradata=1",["apparition","urban"])
a("Aviator Tom Campbell Black at Speke airfield","ghost","","Former Speke Airport hangars, Liverpool","Crowne Plaza Liverpool John Lennon Airport Hotel","Record-breaking pilot Tom Campbell Black died in a runway accident at Speke in 1936, and his shadowy form is reported around the old hangars.","Paranormal Database",PM+"?pageNum_paradata=1",["apparition","urban"])
a("Monk's Well and the chained devil, Wavertree","other","","Monk's Well, Wavertree Green","Wavertree Lock-Up","The old well bears a 1414 Latin inscription warning that the devil below will laugh at those who give nothing; travellers were expected to drink and donate.","Paranormal Database",PM+"?pageNum_paradata=1",["urban","open-to-visit"])
a("Coal-throwing outbreak, Myers Street","poltergeist","1901/03","Myers Street, Smithdown Lane, Liverpool","Smithdown Lane, Liverpool","Windows along the street were smashed by flying lumps of coal, and the breakages carried on even after police began patrolling.","Paranormal Database",PM+"?pageNum_paradata=1",["objects-moved","police","urban"])
a("Phantom city in the sky over Liverpool","other","1846/09/27","Skies over Liverpool","Liverpool Town Hall","A white city briefly appeared above Liverpool; it was put down to a mirage of Edinburgh, although nobody could pick out any of its buildings.","Paranormal Database",PM+"?pageNum_paradata=2",["multiple-witnesses","urban"])
a("Mile-long saucer over Anfield","craft","2007/07/25","Skies over Anfield, Liverpool","Anfield, Liverpool","Lee Jones, his wife and her mother watched a vast saucer hover, partly hidden by cloud; a passing airliner let him estimate it at a mile across. Others reported it earlier that year.","Paranormal Database",PM+"?pageNum_paradata=2",["multiple-witnesses","urban"])
a("Headless horse on Springwood Avenue","ghost","1979/09","Springwood Avenue, Allerton","Springwood Avenue, Liverpool","Two teenage joggers heard hooves behind them and turned to see a headless horse's body draped in something like a tablecloth, which had gone when they looked again.","Paranormal Database",PM+"?pageNum_paradata=2",["road","multiple-witnesses","urban"])
a("Midnight phantom funeral, Knotty Ash","ghost","1891","Thomas Lane, Knotty Ash","Thomas Lane, Liverpool","A witness watched a silent midnight funeral pass, complete with coffin and deathly pale mourners, and later learned a secret funeral had once set out from a nearby hall.","Paranormal Database",PM+"?pageNum_paradata=3",["road","single-witness","urban"])
a("Bus driver's vanishing monk, Walton","ghost","1980","Near St Mary's Church, Walton","St Mary's Church, Walton on the Hill","Driving to work at 3.45am, a bus driver watched a monk cross in front of his car and vanish; he later heard the area was said to be haunted by a monk and nun.","Paranormal Database",PM+"?pageNum_paradata=3",["monk","road","single-witness","church","urban"])
a("Green lantern figure on Woolton Road","ghost","2019","Woolton Road, Allerton","Allerton Cemetery, Liverpool","Walking home late, a witness saw a shadowy figure carrying a green-glowing old lantern cross the road near the cemetery and disappear.","Paranormal Database",PM+"?pageNum_paradata=3",["road","single-witness","urban"])
a("Green lady seen by cadets, Sefton","ghost","1984","Fields by St Helen's Church, Sefton","St Helen's Church, Sefton","At 2.30am one summer night at least four army cadets saw a legless green lady in an old-fashioned dress float across the fields towards the church.","Paranormal Database",PM+"?pageNum_paradata=3",["church","multiple-witnesses","rural","apparition"])
a("Floating sailor of the Punch Bowl, Sefton","ghost","1973","Punch Bowl Inn, Sefton","Punch Bowl, Sefton","A drowned sailor in blue, said to have been laid out in the inn before burial, floats about the building, sometimes just head and shoulders over a mist; he was also seen 'digging' in the churchyard.","Paranormal Database",PM+"?pageNum_paradata=3",["inn","apparition","church"])
a("Rainhill landing chased by police","craft","1978/01","Field near Rainhill, St Helens","Rainhill","Robert Bennett told the St Helens Star he chased a strange craft across the sky with police and radio hams; three officers watched it lift off after landing in a field.","Paranormal Database",PM+"?pageNum_paradata=4",["police","multiple-witnesses","rural"])
a("Stone-throwing on Kirkland Street, St Helens","poltergeist","1905/04","Kirkland Street, St Helens","Kirkland Street, St Helens","For weeks stones, bricks and potatoes rained down on the street after dark, one knocking off a constable's helmet. Police believed a human culprit was responsible.","Paranormal Database",PM+"?pageNum_paradata=4",["objects-moved","police","urban"])
a("Tiny grey figure photographed, Balker Drive","encounter","2021/02/26","Balker Drive, St Helens","Balker Drive, St Helens","A woman testing a new phone camera later found one shot appeared to show a tiny grey alien-like figure walking along the road.","Paranormal Database",PM+"?pageNum_paradata=4",["photo","entity","single-witness","urban"])
# Paranormal Database - Cheshire / Chester
a("Trick-or-treating monk at Chester Cathedral","ghost","2003/10/31","Chester Cathedral, Chester","Chester Cathedral","A grey monk heard speaking old English was seen several times in the 1970s. On Halloween 2003 children offered him their sweet bag and he is said to have eaten the contents, wrappers and all.","Paranormal Database",PC+"?pageNum_paradata=2",["monk","church","child","open-to-visit"])
a("Starved maid of the Bear and Billet","ghost","","Bear and Billet, Lower Bridge Street, Chester","Bear and Billet, Chester","A maid who starved after being locked in a room haunts the stairs and shows herself only to men; mild poltergeist activity and screeches on the answerphone are also reported.","Paranormal Database",PC+"?pageNum_paradata=1",["inn","objects-moved","voices","open-to-visit"])
a("Henrietta at the Blue Bell window","ghost","","Blue Bell Inn, Northgate Street, Chester","Blue Bell, Northgate Street, Chester","Henrietta killed herself in the cellar after learning her Royalist lover died at Rowton Moor; her figure climbs to an upstairs window to wait for him.","Paranormal Database",PC+"?pageNum_paradata=1",["inn","apparition"])
a("Lioness reported at Upton","cryptid","1976/10/23","Upton-by-Chester","Upton-by-Chester","A lioness was reported roaming the Upton area of Chester; police searched but found nothing.","Paranormal Database",PC+"?pageNum_paradata=2",["big-cat","police","urban"])
a("Golden 'leopard cat' shot at, Crewood Hall Farm","cryptid","1981/11","Crewood Hall Farm, Kingsley","Crewood Hall, Kingsley","A farmer said he fired at a large golden cat on his land.","Paranormal Database",PC+"?pageNum_paradata=4",["big-cat","single-witness","rural"])
a("The Thing of Delamere","cryptid","1974","Delamere Forest","Delamere Forest","Locals reported a dog-like animal about 60cm tall with a fox-like tail but an Alsatian look roaming the forest.","Paranormal Database",PC+"?pageNum_paradata=4",["multiple-witnesses","rural"])
a("White lady rising into the trees, Delamere","ghost","2006/07","Delamere Forest, between Frodsham and Delamere station","Delamere railway station","Two walkers heading for Frodsham met a white lady who stared at them for minutes and then floated up into the trees.","Paranormal Database",PC+"?pageNum_paradata=3",["white-lady","multiple-witnesses","rural","open-to-visit"])
a("The Dodleston messages","poltergeist","1984","Meadow Cottage, Dodleston","Dodleston","Thrown objects and rearranged furniture at a cottage were followed by messages appearing on a BBC Micro computer, said to come from several spirits. The case was widely investigated.","Paranormal Database",PC+"?pageNum_paradata=3",["house","objects-moved","investigated","rural"])
a("Headless woman of Hockenhull","ghost","","Bridle path from Hockenhull Hall, near Tarvin","Hockenhull Platts","A servant beheaded by Cromwell's men for hiding her master's treasure walks the old path; she appeared so often that the nearby inn took the name Headless Woman.","Paranormal Database",PC+"?pageNum_paradata=7",["road","rural","inn"])
a("Crying princes at Farndon Bridge","ghost","","Farndon Bridge, River Dee","Farndon Bridge","Two young princes, legend says, were thrown from the bridge by Roger Mortimer, and their cries are heard on stormy nights.","Paranormal Database",PC+"?pageNum_paradata=3",["child","voices","rural","open-to-visit"])
a("Haunted flat above the Frodsham butcher's","poltergeist","2010/04","Main Street, Frodsham","Main Street, Frodsham","A couple spent nights in hotels to escape a presence that lifted bed sheets, slid the shower curtain, shut doors and breathed on the husband's neck.","Paranormal Database",PC+"?pageNum_paradata=3",["house","objects-moved","urban"])
a("Old woman drawn by Reginald Easton, Thurstaston","ghost","","Thurstaston Hall, Thurstaston","Thurstaston Hall","Artist Reginald Easton woke to an old woman by his bed and stayed a week to sketch her; she is said to have murdered a child at the hall.","Paranormal Database",PC+"?pageNum_paradata=7",["house","apparition","single-witness","rural"])
a("Headmaster's ghost at Oldershaw, Wallasey","ghost","","Oldershaw School, Wallasey","Oldershaw Academy, Wallasey","A figure in a headmaster's gown, called Mr McGraw, was seen and heard; one cleaner persuaded the caretaker to arm himself with a pistol and search.","Paranormal Database",PC+"?pageNum_paradata=7",["apparition","urban"])
a("Black lady and dog on Burton Marsh","ghost","","Marsh between Burton and the Harp Inn, Neston","Harp Inn, Little Neston","A woman in black with a black dog was said to cross the Dee marsh at night, a tale perhaps spread by smugglers to keep people away.","Paranormal Database",PC,["black-dog","coast","rural"])
a("The Runcorn poltergeist, Byron Street","poltergeist","1952/08/17","1 Byron Street, Runcorn","Byron Street, Runcorn","For ten weeks in 1952 a house suffered broken items, banging and violently shaking tables, and a seven-foot figure was seen, before it all stopped.","Paranormal Database",PC+"?pageNum_paradata=6",["house","objects-moved","entity","investigated","urban"])
a("Black cloud and dying pigs at Pool Farm","other","1952/08","Pool Farm (now Spur Road), Runcorn","Norton Priory, Runcorn","As 53 pigs died without diagnosis, a three-metre black cloud drifted around the farm, once passing through the pig-shed wall; it was last seen in November.","Paranormal Database",PC+"?pageNum_paradata=6",["rural","physical-traces"])
a("Glowing monks and singing, Norton Priory","ghost","1972","Norton Priory, Runcorn","Norton Priory","A trespasser on the priory ruins said he heard beautiful singing and saw a pair of glowing monks.","Paranormal Database",PC+"?pageNum_paradata=6",["monk","voices","single-witness","open-to-visit"])
a("Fireman Jack of the Old Fire Station","ghost","1960s","Old Fire Station, Northgate Street, Chester","Old Fire Station, Northgate Street, Chester","In the 1960s a bearded phantom fireman in a brass helmet was seen sitting on a ladder; the witness rang the alarm bell and quit soon after.","Paranormal Database",PC+"?pageNum_paradata=1",["apparition","single-witness","urban"])
a("Shape-shifting figure from the canal, Chester","ghost","1959/02/20","Shropshire Union Canal by Griffiths Corn Mill","Steam Mill, Chester","A walker watched a pale grey form rise from the canal, change shape and wrap him in a clammy mist before he broke free and ran.","Paranormal Database",PC+"?pageNum_paradata=1",["entity","single-witness","urban"])
a("Vanishing figures on the Bridge of Sighs","ghost","1990s","Bridge of Sighs, Northgate Street, Chester","Bridge of Sighs, Chester","In the late 1990s a cyclist looked up at the bridge and saw two or three people in old-fashioned clothes who then vanished. Condemned prisoners once crossed it to chapel.","Paranormal Database",PC+"?pageNum_paradata=2",["apparition","single-witness","urban"])
a("Headless Royalist of Tudor House","ghost","","Tudor House, Lower Bridge Street, Chester","Tudor House, Lower Bridge Street, Chester","A Royalist soldier decapitated by a cannon ball while lodging here is said to haunt the house, along with a grey lady.","Paranormal Database",PC+"?pageNum_paradata=2",["house","soldier","grey-lady","urban"])
a("Squeaking phantom bicycle, Saltney Junction","ghost","","Saltney Junction, Chester","Saltney Junction","A railway guard and a child met a bicycle with a squeaking wheel in the early hours that vanished before reaching them; it was linked to a nearby suicide.","Paranormal Database",PC+"?pageNum_paradata=1",["road","multiple-witnesses","urban"])
a("Utkinton Hall spirit trapped in a blackbird","other","","Utkinton Hall, Utkinton","Utkinton Hall","A priest is said to have bound a troublesome spirit into a blackbird, and the hall's blackbirds are said to descend from it.","Paranormal Database",PC+"?pageNum_paradata=7",["house","rural"])
